---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Tragedy of the commons — five small explainers"
  description="One slider showing how a shared fish stock collapses once too many fishers take more than their share."
  accent="green"
  activePath={`${base}tragedy-of-the-commons/`}
>
  <h1>Why everyone fishing "a little more" empties the pond</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    One hundred fishers share a pond. Most fish a sustainable amount, but
    some take a bit more for themselves — a rational choice for any one
    person, since the pond is huge and their own share barely matters.
    Drag the slider and watch what happens once enough people make that
    same rational choice.
  </p>

  <section class="panel" aria-label="Simulation">
    <div class="controls">
      <div class="control">
        <label for="coop-slider"
          >Fishers who fish sustainably <output id="coop-output" for="coop-slider">55%</output
          ></label
        >
        <input type="range" id="coop-slider" min="0" max="100" step="1" value="55" />
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="assumption" id="fisher-breakdown"></p>

    <div class="pond" id="pond" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <svg class="growth-chart" viewBox="0 0 600 200" role="img" aria-labelledby="tc-chart-title">
      <title id="tc-chart-title">Fish stock over 20 rounds</title>
      <polyline id="stock-line" class="line-stock" points="" />
      <line id="round-marker" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="200" class="marker" />
    </svg>

    <p id="round-status" aria-live="polite"></p>
    <p id="outcome-readout" class="outcome" aria-live="polite"></p>
  </section>

  <section class="explainer">
    <h2>Nobody decided to ruin it</h2>
    <p>
      Every fisher who takes a bit more is making a locally sensible call:
      the pond looks huge, one extra catch won't sink it, and if they don't
      take the fish someone else will. The problem is that the same
      reasoning is available to everyone, and the pond can't tell who's
      being greedy — it just adds up every catch and subtracts it from a
      stock that can only regrow so fast. In this model the pond can absorb
      quite a lot of free-riding and still recover, but past roughly two
      thirds of fishers taking more than their share, the total catch
      permanently outruns the regrowth and the stock spirals to zero within
      the twenty rounds shown here. Nobody chose the collapse; it fell out
      of a hundred individually reasonable choices, and once the fish are
      gone, the fishers who were being careful lose exactly as much as the
      ones who weren't.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  import { initTragedyOfCommons } from "../scripts/tragedy-of-commons";
  initTragedyOfCommons();
</script>

<style>
  .pond {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    min-height: 3rem;
    margin-block: var(--space-4);
  }

  .pond-dot {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    transition: opacity 0.15s ease;
  }

  .line-stock {
    stroke: var(--accent);
  }

  #round-status {
    text-align: center;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .outcome {
    font-weight: 600;
    text-align: center;
    min-height: 1.6rem;
  }

  @media (width <= 480px) {
    .pond-dot {
      font-size: 1.15rem;
    }
  }
</style>
